  {
    "sha": "c7eddf281665a36c73928682978f31f208793226",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKGM3ZWRkZjI4MTY2NWEzNmM3MzkyODY4Mjk3OGYzMWYyMDg3OTMyMjY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T22:38:17Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T22:38:17Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(verify): law (b) reads a Boundary-mode arc on its true circle against the walls\n\nOutside Area mode law (b) read an arc move only at its chord joints, so a\nsharp wall or island corner between two joints was never measured: a 4 mm\ncutter on an r 200 arc passed a 90 um gouge with the corner midway between\njoints. In Boundary mode an XY arc now joins the whole-move wall reading\nstraight moves have had since #43, with the exact least distance from each\nwall edge to the arc (sim::verify::arc_wall): the radial distance over the\npart of the edge inside the arc's wedge, else the arc's endpoints. The\nradius band takes the 1 um centre lattice, so the reading never stands\nfarther than the truth. A non-number arc fails closed. Area mode and XZ/YZ\narcs are unchanged.\n\nPinned by boundary_arc_walls (a corner between joints past the floor is a\ngouge, ccw and cw, outside and inside the circle; just inside the floor\nstays clean; Area verdicts unchanged) and\narc_wall::tests::the_exact_distance_matches_a_dense_sampling.\n\nFixes #905\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "33c2c47b7c0e5044b778bf5bdbe85f7ade08960b",
